      "provenance": {
        "notes": "WEAK TOXICITY SOURCE: the only fetched statement is Clemson's general remark that ferns are considered non-toxic to pets; NC State and RHS say nothing, and the ASPCA entry page for this fern could not be read (the fetch returned the landing page). Severity 0 is therefore from_knowledge_verify; treat as unconfirmed until the ASPCA page is read. Watering: Clemson says moisten when the top inch is dry but never let it dry out entirely; NC State and RHS say keep moist. Kept keep_moist. Size is the NC State outdoor-scale figure (3 to 5 ft by 2 to 3 ft; RHS 1 to 1.5 m by 0.5 to 1 m); Clemson says indoor fronds reach 18 to 24 inches. Humidity is high on both NC State and Clemson but no number is given, so unknown."
